# AutoTwin DE — build context filter.
#
# Both images build from the repository root (the uv workspace spans packages/ and
# services/), so this file is what keeps the context from including a multi-gigabyte
# node_modules, an OSM extract and the developer's virtualenv. Anything listed here is also
# invisible to COPY, which is why apps/web/node_modules cannot clobber the pnpm layer in
# infra/docker/web.Dockerfile.

# ---- VCS & CI ----
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ---- Python ----
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov
**/build
**/dist

# ---- Node / Next.js ----
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.pnpm-store
apps/web/playwright-report
apps/web/test-results
apps/web/blob-report

# ---- Data lake and OSM extracts: never part of an image ----
data
*.parquet
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.osm.pbf
*.osrm*

# ---- Local runtime state & docker volumes ----
.volumes
infra/docker/volumes
orchestration/airflow/logs

# ---- Secrets: the image gets its configuration from the environment, never from a file ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets

# ---- Editor / OS noise ----
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Documentation ----
# Only docs/ is dropped. Every README.md stays: uv reads `readme = "README.md"` out of
# each workspace member's pyproject.toml while installing it, and a missing readme is a
# hard metadata error rather than a warning.
docs
